Z||000006||Fformula88||07-23-2001||05:18 PM||||Don't underestimate the 4 bangers in those cars... especially the GT-S.  Although the engine isn't loaded with torque, especially at low RPM's, they have good upper range HP.  The #'s are 180 HP @ 7600 RPM, 130 LB-FT of torque @ 6800<P>Although they do not musclecar type power, they don't have musclecar type weight either.  Motor Trend's test Celica hit 60 in 6.6 seconds!  The 6 speed manual lets you keep those revs up and the car moving along.<P>I haven't driven one, and have seen a lot of reviews saying its not much fun in traffic with stop and go driving, but it looks like it can pick up its pace very fast!  <P>I enjoy big displacement torquey engines more than the high RPM engines, but that doesn't make the car slow either.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
