Z||000013||saleenfiero||07-27-2001||08:53 PM||||The Celica GT-S is a cool car to drive....if you have the standard because the automatic in these cars sucks ROCKS.  It shifts to early and holds back alot of potential.  The 6-speed is better, but you still have to spin the engine up to embarassing speeds to get any performance.  It does suck booting around town, unless you want to be noticed all the damn time, revving the engine.  But with a body kit like this, I guess that's the idea.||||reg||1
Z||000014||artherd||07-28-2001||02:56 AM||||Is it just me, or does this car need MUCH larger wheels, eg 45 series rubber on 18" or so wheels, and the fenders need to be raised to acomodate it?<P>There's almost as much car on TOP of the wheels as there is below...<P>If done right, this would make a very classy, and very fast, project car.  Not a "ricer" but a true racer.  Infact, it'd be intresting indeed to actually race one in a sanctioned event where modifications are allowed and competitive. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
